1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,460
[audience murmuring]

2
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:13,380
[gasps]

3
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:16,420
I'm feeling a bit off today.

4
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:17,920
Oh, are you okay?

5
00:00:18,130 --> 00:00:20,420
Your voice has sounded a
little strange today.

6
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:21,670
My voice sounds strange?

7
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:25,250
Yes, but your beautiful singing
voice shone through like always.

8
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:27,130
Yeah, I guess so.

9
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:29,670
Maybe something's wrong
with the machine, right?

10
00:00:31,330 --> 00:00:32,210
Yeah, maybe.

11
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:36,750
What? You're leaving already?

12
00:00:37,170 --> 00:00:38,330
I want to go for a run.

13
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:40,540
Bye, take care of Lara for me.

14
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:44,380
[sighs]

15
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:49,920
[LARA] It's been 3 weeks
since the tournament.

16
00:00:50,670 --> 00:00:54,250
and since then our relationship
has started to change.

17
00:00:54,710 --> 00:00:55,880
Little by little.

18
00:00:56,790 --> 00:00:58,710
I never would have
imagined that you'd be

19
00:00:58,790 --> 00:01:00,790
the one to meet her
Prince Charming first.

20
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:01,880
Yeah.

21
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:04,000
So tell me about it.

22
00:01:04,710 --> 00:01:06,040
Do you think it's true love?

23
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:12,040
The sunlight is slowly
beginning to shine through,

24
00:01:13,670 --> 00:01:16,830
and the future is beginning to
look brighter than ever before.

25
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:20,830
I'm sure that with this person.

26
00:01:21,290 --> 00:01:23,710
I will finally be able
to find the true love

27
00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:26,130
I've been searching
for all this time.

28
00:01:27,330 --> 00:01:29,380
[♪ soft piano music]

29
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:34,630
[♪ opening music begins]

30
00:02:59,210 --> 00:03:01,170
[♪ opening music ends]

31
00:03:02,830 --> 00:03:03,670
Hmm.

32
00:03:04,290 --> 00:03:06,830
Well, it's nothing like my
potion, that's for sure.

33
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:07,920
It's a fake.

34
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:10,290
But then why do I
feel so much better?

35
00:03:11,170 --> 00:03:13,250
[WITCH] It's basically
just a Band-Aid.

36
00:03:13,670 --> 00:03:15,670
I don't know how
much longer it'll last.

37
00:03:16,290 --> 00:03:17,880
[LARA] Yeah, maybe.

38
00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:20,040
But little by little,
I feel like

39
00:03:20,130 --> 00:03:22,250
I really am getting
closer to true love.

40
00:03:23,080 --> 00:03:24,830
I'm going to see
Luca again today.

41
00:03:26,130 --> 00:03:28,960
So does that mean I'll
see a different ending

42
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:31,250
than the one from 200 years ago?

43
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:32,210
Huh.

44
00:03:33,290 --> 00:03:35,880
Will you finally find
true love this time

45
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:38,830
with this new prince?

46
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:43,750
Luca, my new prince.

47
00:03:44,250 --> 00:03:46,380
[♪ soft piano music]

48
00:03:49,250 --> 00:03:50,420
Hey, please don't move.

49
00:03:51,330 --> 00:03:53,130
How long do I have
to stay like this?

50
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:55,420
[LUCA] It'll be done soon.

51
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:58,080
You said that already and
then started over.

52
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,080
Hey! Look, you can't
rush perfection.

53
00:04:01,630 --> 00:04:03,290
Luca loses interest quickly

54
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:07,460
and sometimes gets sulky
or turns away in a huff.

55
00:04:07,750 --> 00:04:09,750
Why don't you try
using a brighter color?

56
00:04:10,290 --> 00:04:12,170
So when I hear him
called a prince,

57
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,460
I'm not so sure I can agree.

58
00:04:14,670 --> 00:04:15,500
Nice.

59
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:17,330
Although—

60
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:20,750
What's this?

61
00:04:21,630 --> 00:04:22,500
Is it a potion?

62
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:26,210
Well, kinda, in a way. It gives
you energy when you drink it.

63
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,000
[♪ soft guitar music]

64
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:32,830
[drinking heavily]

65
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:34,540
Ah!

66
00:04:41,250 --> 00:04:44,170
[seagulls squawking]

67
00:04:47,380 --> 00:04:50,380
[♪ soft guitar music]

68
00:04:53,380 --> 00:04:54,330
[BOTH] Beautiful.

69
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:03,170
Well, I mean, I— uh,
I'm really sorry about that.

70
00:05:03,750 --> 00:05:05,290
I thought you would like it.

71
00:05:06,330 --> 00:05:09,330
[♪ soft guitar music continues]

72
00:05:11,540 --> 00:05:12,380
[sighs]

73
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:16,380
[LARA] Maybe Luca isn't
a prince after all,

74
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:21,420
but sometimes I catch a glimpse
of the warmth inside him,

75
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:25,500
and it makes my
heart feel so warm.

76
00:05:27,130 --> 00:05:30,630
And then it overflows and
fills my whole chest.

77
00:05:33,630 --> 00:05:35,210
-[MARI] Hmm.
-Huh?

78
00:05:37,330 --> 00:05:40,580
I don't think I was supposed
to hear any of that stuff,

79
00:05:40,670 --> 00:05:42,460
but it sounds
like it's going well.

80
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,830
-[LARA] You think so?
-[MARI] Yeah.

81
00:05:45,330 --> 00:05:47,580
[MARI] Well, I mean, it
sounds to me like that

82
00:05:47,670 --> 00:05:49,830
warm feeling you were
talking about just now.

83
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:53,540
Is that not what...
true love is?

84
00:05:56,710 --> 00:05:58,330
-[LARA] No.
-[MARI] Really?

85
00:05:59,670 --> 00:06:01,000
[LARA] No, that's not it.

86
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:04,000
I've just got that feeling
for some reason.

87
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:07,500
But even if I can't explain
what true love actually is,

88
00:06:08,130 --> 00:06:09,380
I know I'll find out soon,

89
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:11,500
as long as I'm with Luca.

90
00:06:13,330 --> 00:06:15,210
[♪ cheerful music]

91
00:06:16,330 --> 00:06:18,500
-I'm here to cause trouble!
-[LARA] Leo!

92
00:06:19,210 --> 00:06:21,540
I'm sorry. My parents had
something to do today.

93
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:23,920
[LARA] Mm-mm.
I'm so happy to see her.

94
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:27,130
That's right. You two better
take good care of me today.

95
00:06:27,250 --> 00:06:28,830
-[Leo laughs]
-[LUCA] Yeah, yeah.

96
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:31,380
[♪ cheerful music]

97
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:46,380
[sigh]

98
00:06:47,290 --> 00:06:48,500
[Luca pants]

99
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:52,380
I'm gonna... I'm gonna get us
something to drink.

100
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:54,460
[panting]

101
00:06:58,210 --> 00:06:59,920
So spill it, do you
like my brother?

102
00:07:00,540 --> 00:07:01,380
Huh?

103
00:07:02,210 --> 00:07:03,830
-Uhum.
-Wow.

104
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:06,380
So does that mean
you two are dating?

105
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:07,710
Oh, dating?

106
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:12,330
-Not yet, huh?
-What do you mean?

107
00:07:14,170 --> 00:07:17,380
I'm not a little kid. You don't
have to play dumb with me, okay?

108
00:07:19,540 --> 00:07:21,000
But that sounds about right.

109
00:07:21,330 --> 00:07:23,460
My older brother is
such a scaredy-cat.

110
00:07:24,250 --> 00:07:26,080
So what do you want to be, Lara?

111
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:28,500
-To be?
-Yeah.

112
00:07:29,790 --> 00:07:32,750
If you're waiting for him to
make the first move, you'll be

113
00:07:32,830 --> 00:07:33,880
waiting for a while.

114
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:35,750
[gasps]

115
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:39,710
Leo, you look like you're about
to say something you shouldn't.

116
00:07:40,670 --> 00:07:42,130
[LEO] Did you buy that again?

117
00:07:42,710 --> 00:07:44,380
[LUCA] Well, it's good, right?

118
00:07:46,420 --> 00:07:49,290
[LARA] And then... while we
were on our way home,

119
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:52,040
I couldn't get it
out of my head.

120
00:07:53,830 --> 00:07:55,080
I'm going to be waiting.

121
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:57,170
I'm going to be waiting.

122
00:07:58,710 --> 00:08:01,460
I wonder if I'll be waiting
forever for true love.

123
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:10,500
Oh, hey, can you tell me
what true love really is?

124
00:08:10,790 --> 00:08:11,960
[EMA] You're burning it!

125
00:08:12,250 --> 00:08:13,080
[gasps]

126
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:17,330
-It's done!
-You did it!

127
00:08:17,710 --> 00:08:19,380
[MAKOTO] So, say that again.

128
00:08:20,330 --> 00:08:21,960
-True love?
-[LARA] Yeah.

129
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:23,540
[YOSHI] What a topic. Sounds

130
00:08:23,630 --> 00:08:25,420
-just like Lara.
-[MAKOTO] My mom might

131
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:27,710
-have some wisdom on this.
-[LARA] Is that so?

132
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:30,330
-Well, she's a pastor.
-A pastor?

133
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:32,420
Okay, let's see.

134
00:08:32,710 --> 00:08:34,330
Are you dating that boy?

135
00:08:34,710 --> 00:08:36,380
The one I see around a lot,

136
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:38,000
the slender, fair-skinned guy?

137
00:08:38,130 --> 00:08:40,750
Huh? What?
Is he your boyfriend?

138
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:42,210
What's a boyfriend?

139
00:08:43,290 --> 00:08:44,210
[EMA] So are you?

140
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:47,330
I don't know.
Leo asked me that too.

141
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:48,380
[YOSHI] Who's Leo?

142
00:08:48,710 --> 00:08:49,880
[MARI] Reel it in, man.

143
00:08:50,830 --> 00:08:53,040
I don't think I understand.

144
00:08:54,170 --> 00:08:57,630
[LARA] Do you have to date
someone to find true love?

145
00:08:58,460 --> 00:08:59,960
Well, usually, but not always.

146
00:09:00,630 --> 00:09:03,330
There are things you can only
understand by dating.

147
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,830
You have to tell each
other how you feel

148
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:07,960
and discover the
shape of your love.

149
00:09:08,670 --> 00:09:10,170
Otherwise, move forward.

150
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,790
The shape of our love.

151
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:15,250
[MAKOTO] Right.
Back in my day—

152
00:09:15,330 --> 00:09:16,210
[YOSHI] Here we go.

153
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:18,040
[MARI] Oh no, not another story.

154
00:09:18,420 --> 00:09:20,830
-Dad, is this done yet?
-Oh, I'll take care of it.

155
00:09:21,170 --> 00:09:23,920
[EMA] Well, Lara,
I hope that was helpful.

156
00:09:24,250 --> 00:09:26,500
-[MAKOTO] Oh! Oh...
-[EMA] What are you doing?

157
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:27,580
Sorry, sorry.

158
00:09:27,750 --> 00:09:29,330
-Wow—
-Should, I check the breaker?

159
00:09:29,420 --> 00:09:30,790
-[EMA] Please do!
-[MAKOTO] Oh,

160
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:32,330
-my phone.
-[EMA] I'll get mine,

161
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:33,250
just wait a sec.

162
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:36,460
[rope swishes]

163
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:43,000
If you are looking for Lara

164
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:45,290
she's working today. Huh?

165
00:09:46,210 --> 00:09:48,000
[faucet running]

166
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:54,960
[♪ soft piano music]

167
00:09:58,830 --> 00:10:00,580
So, what happened?

168
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:02,830
Hmm.

169
00:10:04,290 --> 00:10:05,130
I don't know.

170
00:10:05,630 --> 00:10:07,540
Lara's still a mystery, I guess.

171
00:10:08,420 --> 00:10:11,500
Every time I try to get close
to her and try to get to

172
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:14,290
know her better, she
feels even farther away.

173
00:10:15,710 --> 00:10:18,580
When I look at her, I get
the feeling that there's

174
00:10:18,670 --> 00:10:21,040
something inside her that
she can't show anyone.

175
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:25,710
And it feels like—
I've never actually... seen

176
00:10:25,790 --> 00:10:28,250
the real Lara before, you know?

177
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:32,130
And whenever it seems I'm
getting close, she disappears.

178
00:10:34,130 --> 00:10:36,420
[leaves rustling]

179
00:10:36,790 --> 00:10:38,080
Thanks for listening to me.

180
00:10:38,420 --> 00:10:39,790
Sorry I said weird stuff.

181
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:44,330
I'm going to say
something weird too.

182
00:10:45,170 --> 00:10:46,540
I think you're a good guy.

183
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:48,290
Huh?

184
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:51,460
And thanks to you, Lara's back.

185
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:55,130
You've always been there
for her, even when she

186
00:10:55,210 --> 00:10:56,960
can't be there for herself.

187
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:01,460
Lara can only move forward
little by little, so it's hard

188
00:11:01,540 --> 00:11:02,880
to understand and hard

189
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:05,250
to see, but I think
it's going to work out.

190
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:09,580
I really do, because you
have a great connection.

191
00:11:12,250 --> 00:11:13,080
Thanks.

192
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:15,790
Um, Mari?

193
00:11:17,420 --> 00:11:21,040
From your perspective, what
kind of person is Lara?

194
00:11:22,630 --> 00:11:24,330
She's an idiot,
a little clueless,

195
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:25,960
and she's someone I care about.

196
00:11:27,250 --> 00:11:29,750
You should definitely
go out with him. I mean it!

197
00:11:30,130 --> 00:11:32,290
You absolutely
definitely should!

198
00:11:32,580 --> 00:11:34,830
Come on, that guy is totally
into you, Lara.

199
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:36,790
I really hope that's true.

200
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:41,380
Well, someone confessed his
feelings to me the other day.

201
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:42,880
Oh! Yeah? Ouji?

202
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:46,750
Oh no, it was nerve-wracking,
but it made me happy.

203
00:11:47,250 --> 00:11:50,630
Having someone tell you that
they like you is way more

204
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:52,920
wonderful than
I was originally expecting.

205
00:11:53,710 --> 00:11:56,290
Okay, so what happens now then?

206
00:11:57,290 --> 00:11:58,130
Actually...

207
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:01,250
we're dating now.

208
00:12:02,250 --> 00:12:04,420
[♪ melancholic piano music]

209
00:12:06,750 --> 00:12:08,500
You're going to be
waiting a while.

210
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:11,250
You have to discover the
shape of your love.

211
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:15,420
If it's true that
expressing my feelings

212
00:12:16,420 --> 00:12:18,040
can give shape to love...

213
00:12:19,750 --> 00:12:21,710
If it can really help
me find the true

214
00:12:21,790 --> 00:12:23,540
love that I've been
searching for,

215
00:12:26,460 --> 00:12:29,040
then I have no choice
but to keep going.

216
00:12:30,130 --> 00:12:31,290
Before it's too late.

217
00:12:32,250 --> 00:12:34,420
[printer whirring]

218
00:12:41,130 --> 00:12:41,960
[beeping]

219
00:12:43,750 --> 00:12:45,830
[clock ticking]

220
00:12:48,130 --> 00:12:50,960
[LISA] If only the witch
would just disappear forever.

221
00:12:55,380 --> 00:12:57,170
[water sloshing]

222
00:12:59,750 --> 00:13:00,580
What's wrong?

223
00:13:01,580 --> 00:13:03,500
She's been sleeping
all the time lately.

224
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:06,500
I think she's
not feeling well.

225
00:13:07,460 --> 00:13:08,290
Lady Witch?

226
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:11,790
-[MARI] Yeah.
-[LARA] Is she going to be okay?

227
00:13:12,750 --> 00:13:15,130
Now, let's try changing the
water in the tank.

228
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:19,710
When we first met, she looked
like she was about to die... but

229
00:13:19,790 --> 00:13:21,880
she perked right
up once I set up the tank.

230
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:24,460
But she did complain
nonstop about it being

231
00:13:24,540 --> 00:13:25,790
too small and stuff.

232
00:13:26,330 --> 00:13:27,460
It was a real hassle.

233
00:13:27,710 --> 00:13:30,580
She's super picky about
the substrate and plants too,

234
00:13:30,790 --> 00:13:32,920
and if temperature isn't
kept slightly low,

235
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:33,960
she gets all grumpy.

236
00:13:34,170 --> 00:13:36,830
It sounds like you know
everything about her, don't you?

237
00:13:37,670 --> 00:13:38,830
I know more than that.

238
00:13:39,580 --> 00:13:42,040
Like how she gets mouthy
when she's in a good mood.

239
00:13:42,170 --> 00:13:43,210
You're so noisy!

240
00:13:44,130 --> 00:13:45,790
You guys, ah!
Really?

241
00:13:46,880 --> 00:13:48,670
Could you at least keep
it down? It's—

242
00:13:48,750 --> 00:13:49,580
I think...

243
00:13:50,290 --> 00:13:51,790
she'll be better in no time.

244
00:13:54,130 --> 00:13:56,540
[♪ soft piano music]

245
00:13:58,580 --> 00:14:01,710
[LARA] I think I'll tell Luca
how I feel tomorrow.

246
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:13,330
If I...

247
00:14:14,290 --> 00:14:15,460
tell him how I feel...

248
00:14:16,330 --> 00:14:18,330
and he returns those feelings.

249
00:14:19,330 --> 00:14:21,540
Surely that can be
the start of true love,

250
00:14:23,330 --> 00:14:24,460
and that will be that.

251
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:26,710
I won't have to wait any longer.

252
00:14:27,750 --> 00:14:30,380
[♪ soft piano music continues]

253
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:35,040
[MARI] That'll work out,
definitely.

254
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:42,710
[WITCH] In life, we are
actually born twice.

255
00:14:43,170 --> 00:14:44,000
[gasps]

256
00:14:44,710 --> 00:14:47,670
The first time we are born,
it is simply to exist.

257
00:14:48,210 --> 00:14:50,830
The second time we are
born, we begin to live.

258
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:52,750
That so?

259
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:02,420
Lady Witch...

260
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:06,920
I'm so glad.

261
00:15:07,630 --> 00:15:10,330
I'm so glad I made the decision
to come here after all.

262
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:13,290
-Thank you.
-Hmm.

263
00:15:18,130 --> 00:15:18,960
This is...?

264
00:15:19,880 --> 00:15:22,670
Something I extracted from
the traces left in the mansion.

265
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:25,830
I think it likely
belongs to the witch,

266
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:26,830
[gasps]

267
00:15:27,290 --> 00:15:31,250
...and if that's the case,
then she is no longer a mermaid,

268
00:15:31,750 --> 00:15:33,250
but she isn't a human either.

269
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:39,000
[♪ ethereal music begins]

270
00:15:55,540 --> 00:15:57,540
True love may
elude me currently,

271
00:15:59,040 --> 00:16:03,250
but in my search for it, I have
stumbled upon something else.

272
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:05,130
Something valuable.

273
00:16:07,830 --> 00:16:12,210
I've met so many amazing people
who are irreplaceable to me now

274
00:16:16,250 --> 00:16:17,960
and the one destined for me.

275
00:16:18,420 --> 00:16:19,250
Ready?

276
00:16:20,710 --> 00:16:21,790
It's gonna be sunny.

277
00:16:23,130 --> 00:16:26,330
Perhaps what I was really
searching for this whole time

278
00:16:27,290 --> 00:16:28,540
wasn't just true love.

279
00:16:29,330 --> 00:16:30,710
But a greater understanding.

280
00:16:31,250 --> 00:16:33,420
An understanding of
these feelings I have

281
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,130
for this world we live in.

282
00:16:37,920 --> 00:16:40,790
Today, I'm sure I'll find
out what it all means

283
00:16:41,330 --> 00:16:42,920
once and for all.

284
00:16:47,790 --> 00:16:50,330
[EMA] I wish you'd kept
playing the organ.

285
00:16:50,750 --> 00:16:52,790
What do I need to do to
have girls like me?

286
00:16:53,040 --> 00:16:55,080
[EMA] You don't need anything.

287
00:16:55,380 --> 00:16:57,420
Then how come no one
likes me, huh?

288
00:16:58,330 --> 00:17:01,920
Come on now, I like you
and you know that.

289
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:04,750
[YOSHI] That's not what I mean.

290
00:17:07,250 --> 00:17:09,380
[♪ ethereal music ends]

291
00:17:13,630 --> 00:17:14,460
Lara?

292
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:17,830
[LARA] Hey, there's
something that...

293
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:20,040
I want to tell you.

294
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,500
I want to be your
girlfriend, Luca.

295
00:17:30,330 --> 00:17:32,380
[flapping wings]

296
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:43,130
[LUCA] I'm so happy.

297
00:17:44,170 --> 00:17:45,880
I want that as well.

298
00:17:46,460 --> 00:17:47,290
[gasps]

299
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:54,130
[magical sound]

300
00:17:59,330 --> 00:18:01,170
-[LARA] That's it?
-[LUCA] Huh?

301
00:18:06,710 --> 00:18:07,580
[sighs]

302
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:17,250
[LARA] Luca?

303
00:18:20,830 --> 00:18:22,580
Oh no, I'm sorry!

304
00:18:23,210 --> 00:18:25,580
I'm just— I'm a little nervous.

305
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:28,420
You're really important
to me, and I just want us

306
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:30,920
to take our time
and make sure we get this right.

307
00:18:31,250 --> 00:18:33,710
Take it slow! Can we just
take it little by little?

308
00:18:35,580 --> 00:18:36,630
Little by little?

309
00:18:39,250 --> 00:18:40,920
[magical sound]

310
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:43,920
[gasps]

311
00:18:44,500 --> 00:18:45,330
[sighs]

312
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:47,960
So, then when?

313
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:49,830
Huh?

314
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:52,000
What do you mean?

315
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:54,500
I'm just saying that we should

316
00:18:54,580 --> 00:18:56,330
probably take it
slow for a while.

317
00:18:57,540 --> 00:18:59,250
But how long will
I have to wait?

318
00:19:01,630 --> 00:19:02,630
[sobs]

319
00:19:03,250 --> 00:19:04,630
[WITCH] Lara... wait!

320
00:19:06,040 --> 00:19:06,880
You...

321
00:19:10,250 --> 00:19:11,790
I can't just wait
around for you.

322
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:13,460
I, I don't have any time left.

323
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:16,210
If I wait, it'll never happen.

324
00:19:16,830 --> 00:19:17,670
[sighs]

325
00:19:17,790 --> 00:19:20,920
Lisa was right.
I'll never have true love.

326
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:22,580
[sobbing]
It'll never happen.

327
00:19:23,830 --> 00:19:24,670
Lara...

328
00:19:26,130 --> 00:19:28,420
It has to be right now.
Don't you understand?

329
00:19:29,080 --> 00:19:29,920
Luca!

330
00:19:31,130 --> 00:19:31,960
Huh?

331
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:37,040
[LUCA] What? Lara,
I don't understand.

332
00:19:38,130 --> 00:19:40,500
What are you talking about?
True love?

333
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,460
[♪ melancholic music begins]

334
00:19:57,170 --> 00:19:58,580
[magical sound]

335
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:01,790
[chimes]

336
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:07,040
[magical energy spreading]

337
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:20,330
[gasps]

338
00:20:22,500 --> 00:20:23,330
Lara?

339
00:20:23,710 --> 00:20:26,130
[jaw creaks]

340
00:20:27,580 --> 00:20:28,420
What's wrong?

341
00:20:28,670 --> 00:20:29,500
[gasps]

342
00:20:30,210 --> 00:20:32,380
[♪ woman singing]

343
00:20:34,250 --> 00:20:36,080
[magical energy spreading]

344
00:20:36,580 --> 00:20:37,420
[gasps]

345
00:20:38,290 --> 00:20:39,130
Let's go!

346
00:20:40,790 --> 00:20:41,630
Damn it!

347
00:20:45,330 --> 00:20:46,170
[gasps]

348
00:20:54,040 --> 00:20:54,880
[gasps]

349
00:20:56,460 --> 00:20:57,290
Farewell,

350
00:20:58,630 --> 00:20:59,460
Mari.

351
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:00,750
[gasps]

352
00:21:01,670 --> 00:21:02,500
Ah!

353
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,920
[♪ melancholic music continues]

354
00:21:14,170 --> 00:21:15,000
[gasps]

355
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:18,710
Whoa.

356
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:21,750
What the—

357
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:26,710
Hey!

358
00:21:28,540 --> 00:21:31,540
[♪ woman continues singing]

359
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:36,080
Hey, wait, stop!

360
00:21:39,330 --> 00:21:40,500
[magical sound]

361
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:55,630
[♪ closing music begins]

362
00:23:19,750 --> 00:23:21,790
[♪ closing music ends]

363
00:23:29,330 --> 00:23:30,750
[phone buzzes]

364
00:23:32,170 --> 00:23:34,330
Mari! Lara, someone has
taken her! I don't know

365
00:23:34,420 --> 00:23:36,130
where they went!
They just flew off!

366
00:23:36,210 --> 00:23:37,540
Never seen anything like it!

367
00:23:37,630 --> 00:23:38,460
Lara!

368
00:23:40,540 --> 00:23:42,330
Lady Grace,
in your condition—

369
00:23:43,540 --> 00:23:46,420
Ah! Will you just shut up and
give me a hand?!

370
00:23:48,790 --> 00:23:49,880
[LISA] Kota, hurry up!

371
00:23:51,420 --> 00:23:54,380
The witch is on her way to
Ogishima with Lara right now!

372
00:23:56,540 --> 00:23:57,380
[cracks]

